# Drafted by Gemini (R15 sinner), edited.

~ invite
set sinner_roll_started
quest withered_arm roll_the_bones
cutscene dc_roll_bones
Narrator: The room stretches out like old taffy, the ceiling lifting while a four-legged coffin carved with a dice-eyed skeleton settles between you.
cutscene dc_roll_bones_2
Narrator: Across the green felt, his yellow grin catches the lantern light while his hollow-eyed crew crowds close at his back.
cutscene end
mister_crossroads [smile]: Welcome, honoured guests, to my humble parlour. Sit yourselves down, rest your boots, and let a simple sinner propose a friendly wager.
-> invite_menu

~ invite_again
mister_crossroads [smile]: There is no hurry on the river, friends. The felt is brushed, the ivory is warm, and your chairs are waiting.
-> invite_menu

~ invite_menu
* Ask about Adela -> invite_adela
* [Insight DC 20] Judge whether he will keep his word -> invite_insight | invite_insight_miss
* Take the table -> table_play
* Not yet -> invite_refuse
* Draw steel and fight -> sinner_fight

~ invite_adela
mister_crossroads [sly]: Lady Adela's ring and her recovery are right here on the cloth, beside my boat and every poor soul aboard, against your own bright spirits.
mister_crossroads [smile]: Should the stakes feel a touch steep, you are always welcome to take a purse of river gold and walk away happy.
-> invite_menu

~ invite_insight
Narrator: For all his soft manners, his tail twitches hard against the floorboards. He cannot bear to lose, and he will never pay out.
mister_crossroads [smile]: Haha, you look at me like a tax collector inspecting the ledgers. I assure you, my word is as solid as cypress heartwood.
-> invite_menu

~ invite_insight_miss
Narrator: He pours himself a glass of dark rum and tips the bottle toward you, every inch the easygoing riverboat captain.
-> invite_menu

~ invite_refuse
mister_crossroads [smile]: Take all the time you please to enjoy the music and the night air. My table is not going anywhere.
-> END

~ table_play
set dice_score = 0
mister_crossroads [smile]: A dry throat and a bold heart, that is what the river likes. For every chair you fill, I shall set another bone under my cup.
mister_crossroads [sly]: I am a man of large appetites, friends, so do not expect me to bid small.
-> sdice_round1

~ sdice_round1
Narrator: The cups rattle like dry reeds, and he opens the first hand by calling a bold, improbable stack of sixes.
* [Insight DC 16] Hard read: study his grin for the cup's story -> s1_ok | s1_miss
* [Sleight of Hand DC 17] Deft hands: nudge a die -> s1_ok | s1_caught
* [Deception DC 17] Poker face: bluff a big bid -> s1_ok | s1_miss
* Bid cautiously -> s1_miss

~ s1_ok
set dice_score += 1
Narrator: His yellow eyes narrow a fraction as you call the table right, and he sweeps one of his own carved bones into the pot.
-> sdice_round2

~ s1_miss
Narrator: He lifts his cup with a deep, warm chuckle, showing the exact count he boasted while you surrender a die.
-> sdice_round2

~ s1_caught
Narrator: He clicks his tongue gently against his teeth, tapping a clawed finger on the felt before claiming the hand for the house.
-> sdice_round2

~ sdice_round2
Narrator: The leather cups slam down a second time, and he leans forward, raising the call before the ivory even stops spinning.
* [Insight DC 16] Hard read: study his grin for the cup's story -> s2_ok | s2_miss
* [Sleight of Hand DC 17] Deft hands: nudge a die -> s2_ok | s2_caught
* [Deception DC 17] Poker face: bluff a big bid -> s2_ok | s2_miss
* Bid cautiously -> s2_miss

~ s2_ok
set dice_score += 1
Narrator: A muscle jumps in his scaly jaw when the cups rise in your favour, costing him another bone from his pile.
-> sdice_round3

~ s2_miss
Narrator: The ivory shows nothing but bad news for your side of the cloth, and his belly laugh shakes the hanging lamps.
-> sdice_round3

~ s2_caught
Narrator: He shakes his head with fatherly disappointment, clicks his tongue, and rakes the round neatly to his side of the wood.
-> sdice_round3

~ sdice_round3
Narrator: Sweat beads on the brass lamps as the final cups come down hard, and he calls a high, reckless number across the baize.
* [Insight DC 16] Hard read: study his grin for the cup's story -> s3_ok | s3_miss
* [Sleight of Hand DC 17] Deft hands: nudge a die -> s3_ok | s3_caught
* [Deception DC 17] Poker face: bluff a big bid -> s3_ok | s3_miss
* Bid cautiously -> s3_miss

~ s3_ok
set dice_score += 1
Narrator: You catch him out in the cold one last time, and the grin freezes on his snout as his hand falls short.
-> sdice_result

~ s3_miss
Narrator: He turns his cup over with a flourish of his cuffs, and the bones sit smiling up at him in neat, cruel rows.
-> sdice_result

~ s3_caught
Narrator: He gives a polite little click of his tongue, wagging one claw at your cuff before taking the final pot.
-> sdice_result

~ sdice_result
Narrator: The leather cups lift one last time, leaving the pale ivory exposed on the green cloth.
if flag.dice_score >= 2
-> table_win
else
-> table_lose
endif

~ table_win
set sinner_dice = "won"
set jack_boon = 1
Narrator: His last die vanishes, and the four-legged coffin shudders hard, sliding two ghostly numbers into your palms to spend when steel is drawn.
mister_crossroads [angry]: Cheaters and river thieves at my own table. Nobody cleans out this house while I still draw breath.
-> sinner_fight

~ table_lose
set sinner_dice = "lost"
mister_crossroads [smile]: Well played, my dear friends, though luck is a fickle lady on the black water. Now hold still while I collect my winnings.
Narrator: He rises from his chair and hefts a massive blunderbuss etched with weeping sigils, aiming the wide brass barrel across the felt.
-> sinner_fight

~ sinner_fight
cutscene dc_all_in
Narrator: All around the hall, his crew drops to its knees and shrivels like dry leaves, their pale light pouring straight into his gun.
cutscene dc_all_in_2
Narrator: The tall windows shatter inward in a spray of glass and black swamp water as the bayou rushes into the room.
cutscene end
quest withered_arm bayou_boogie
move dc_casino:from_hall

~ ship_bottle
Narrator: Inside the green glass sits a miniature Dead Man's Hand, flying a black flag no bigger than a fingernail painted with a crocodile skull.
-> END

~ desk
Narrator: The dark wood is scored deep with jinxcraft sigils that make your eyes water and your teeth ache if you stare too long.
-> END

~ coffin
Narrator: Snake Eye Jack's coffin stands on four carved legs, and the pair of bone dice resting on its lid always turns up double ones.
-> END

~ after
cutscene dc_jack_due
Narrator: The coffin lid flies wide, and a tangle of skeletal arms and shadow snakes boils out around a tall, laughing shade of magenta light.
cutscene dc_jack_due_2
Narrator: The lid slams shut with the crack of a pistol shot, leaving a fresh crocodile skull and crossbones gouged deep into the wood.
cutscene dc_jack_due_3
Narrator: Shadows settle back over the quiet hall where the Sinner's body slumps in his coat, wide eyes fixed on nothing and the cold gun in his lap.
cutscene end
set grinning_sinner_slain
set sinner_after_seen
-> farewell

~ farewell
if flag.elias_freed
elias_greaves [weary]: The crew is turning to river dust, and the folks at the tables are finally waking up. I am glad I lived to see the morning, friends.
else
Narrator: The old thralls let out a long, dusty sigh before crumbling to ash, while the patrons blink their glassy eyes and ask what time it is.
endif
Narrator: The borrowed luck fades from your fingers and the brass band falls silent, leaving only the smell of spilled rum and gunsmoke.
set act2_done += 1
xp milestone
quest withered_arm return
set crossroads_done
-> END
